{"name":"Lily of the Nile","hex":"#9191bb","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lily","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowers in the genus Lilium of the family Liliaceae, which includes a great many ornamental species.","Any of several species of herbaceous flower which may or may not resemble the genus Lilium in some way, and which are not closely related to it or each other."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["White ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lily of the Nile","blocks":[{"text":"Lily of the Nile is a common name for several plants and may refer to:"},{"items":["Agapanthus africanus","Agapanthus praecox","Zantedeschia aethiopica"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lily_of_the_Nile","wikidata":"Q6548590"},{"title":"Nile","blocks":[{"text":"The Nile is a major north-flowing river in northeast Africa which empties into the Mediterranean Sea. At 7,088 kilometers (4,404 mi) long, it is the longest river in the world, although the volume of water it carries is much smaller than other major rivers such as the Amazon or the Congo. The Nile has played a central role in the environmental, economic, and cultural history of Africa for millennia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Beautiful_nature_along_Nile_River_01.jpg/330px-Beautiful_nature_along_Nile_River_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nile","wikidata":"Q3392"},{"title":"Agapanthus","blocks":[{"text":"Agapanthus is a genus of plants, the only one in the subfamily Agapanthoideae of the family Amaryllidaceae. The subfamily was formerly treated as a separate family, Agapanthaceae. The family is in the monocot order Asparagales. The name is derived from Ancient Greek ἀγάπη (agápē), meaning \"love\", and ἄνθος (ánthos), meaning \"flower\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/